#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:41
msgid "Steps applied to what you say"
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:42
msgid ""
"The processing steps that are switched on, by their ids, in the order they "
"run: field-fit, clean-up, translation, then script conversion. Nothing "
"switched on types exactly what you say. Any step is shown on screen while "
"you speak and typed a sentence at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:52
msgid "Settings of the steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:53
msgid ""
"What each step is set to, keyed step.setting, for example translate.to for "
"the language to translate into, and script.mode for how Chinese is written."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:62
msgid "Keep a record of what was changed"
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:63
msgid ""
"Save what was heard and what was typed, to check what Myna changed. The "
"record holds your words and stays on this computer."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:71
msgid "Sounds on start, stop and error"
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:72
msgid ""
"Play a short sound when dictation starts listening, when it stops, and when "
"it fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:80
msgid "Sound style"
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:81
msgid ""
"Which sounds play: Chime is a struck bar, Bird whistled chirps, Voice the "
"hums people make while listening, Marimba a rising fifth, Water falling "
"drops, Radio a walkie-talkie and Strings a plucked koto."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:90
msgid "When to transcribe"
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:91
msgid ""
"As you speak shows partial text in the field while you talk; When you stop "
"injects the whole transcript once the utterance ends."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:99
msgid "Spoken language"
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:100
msgid ""
"A BCP-47-ish code (en, fr, zh) for the language you dictate in. The model "
"skips language detection and decodes in this language; a code that does not "
"match what is spoken degrades the transcript. Empty lets the model decide."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:110
msgid "Indicator style"
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:111
msgid ""
"All three render the same calibrated audio envelope: Default is a level bar "
"in the accent colour, Ribbon a flowing GPU wave, VU meter a segmented meter."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:121
msgid "Stop after silence (seconds)"
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:122
msgid ""
"With tap-to-start activation, end the dictation session on its own after "
"this many seconds without speech. 0 keeps it running until the next tap. "
"Hold-to-talk always ends with the key."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:131
msgid "Vocabulary"
msgstr ""

#: ../data/glib-2.0/schemas/com.canonical.Myna.Dictation.gschema.xml:132
msgid ""
"Names and terms you use that speech recognition might get wrong, such as a "
"colleague's name, a product or a term from your field: \"Nguyen\", "
"\"Kubernetes\", \"ibuprofen\". To choose how something is written, type what "
"you say, an arrow with a space on each side, then what to write: \"my sequel "
"=> MySQL\". Up to 100 words or short phrases."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.canonical.Myna.Config.metainfo.xml:9
msgid "Set up and configure local dictation"
msgstr ""

#: data/com.canonical.Myna.Config.metainfo.xml:14
msgid ""
"Myna turns speech into text on your computer, with no audio or text leaving "
"it. Myna Settings guides you through installing it and a speech model, then "
"configures dictation and its speech models."
msgstr ""

